a Quality (GOOD) | 94.6% |\\n\\n### 3.2 Asset Inventory\\n\\n| Asset ID | Type | Zone |\\n|----------|------|------|\\n| PUMP-001 | Pump | Zone-A |\\n| PUMP-002 | Pump | Zone-A |\\n| PUMP-003 | Pump | Zone-B |\\n| MOTOR-001 | Motor | Zone-B |\\n| MOTOR-002 | Motor | Zone-C |\\n| FAN-001 | Fan | Zone-C |\\n| FAN-002 | Fan | Zone-A |\\n| COMP-001 | Compressor | Zone-B |\\n\\n### 3.3 Data Quality\\n\\nQuality flag distribution indicates reliable sensor operation:\\n- GOOD: 5,633 observations (94.6%)\\n- WARNING: 209 observations (3.5%)\\n- ERROR: 110 observations (1.9%)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Results\\n\\n### 4.1 Vibration Time Series Analysis\\n\\n![Vibration Time Series](images/vibration_time_series.png)\\n\\nFigure 1 displays vibration RMS values over the 31-day monitoring period for all assets. Notable observations:\\n\\n- COMP-001 consistently operates at elevated vibration levels compared to other assets\\n- PUMP-002 shows progressive increase beginning around day 15-16\\n- Motor assets (MOTOR-001, MOTOR-002) demonstrate the most stable vibration profiles\\n\\n### 4.2 Vibration Distribution by Asset\\n\\n![Vibration by Asset](images/vibration_by_asset.png)\\n\\nFigure 2 presents box plot comparison of vibration distributions across assets:\\n\\n| Asset | Mean (mm/s) | Std Dev | Min | Max |\\n|-------|-------------|---------|-----|-----|\\n| COMP-001 | 4.57 | 1.16 | 1.59 | 8.22 |\\n| FAN-002 | 3.11 | 0.62 | 1.27 | 4.88 |\\n| FAN-001 | 3.08 | 0.62 | 1.44 | 5.25 |\\n| PUMP-002 | 2.83 | 0.73 | 1.11 | 5.21 |\\n| PUMP-001 | 2.40 | 0.50 | 1.16 | 3.85 |\\n| PUMP-003 | 2.40 | 0.48 | 0.96 | 3.87 |\\n| MOTOR-001 | 1.75 | 0.37 | 0.67 | 2.69 |\\n| MOTOR-002 | 1.73 | 0.35 | 0.67 | 2.81 |\\n\\n**Key Finding**: COMP-001 mean vibration (4.57 mm/s) exceeds the fleet average (2.73 mm/s) by 67%, warranting priority investigation.\\n\\n### 4.3 Vibration Distribution by Zone\\n\\n![Vibration by Zone](images/vibration_by_zone.png)\\n\\nZone-level aggregation reveals:\\n\\n| Zone | Mean (mm/s) | Std Dev | Min | Max |\\n|------|-------------|---------|-----|-----|\\n| Zone-B | 2.90 | 1.42 | 0.67 | 8.22 |\\n| Zone-A | 2.78 | 0.69 | 1.11 | 5.21 |\\n| Zone-C | 2.41 | 0.84 | 0.67 | 5.25 |\\n\\nZone-B exhibits highest variability due to COMP-001 presence.\\n\\n### 4.4 Peak Acceleration Analysis\\n\\n![Peak Acceleration Distribution](images/peak_accel_distribution.png)\\n\\nPeak acceleration values show strong correlation with RMS vibration (r=0.94), confirming consistent measurement characteristics. COMP-001 reaches maximum peak values of 29.1g, significantly above other assets.\\n\\n### 4.5 Degradation Trend Analysis\\n\\n![Degradation Trend](images/degradation_trend.png)\\n\\nDaily mean vibration for assets showing degradation patterns:\\n\\n**PUMP-002 Trend**:\\n- Days 1-15: Mean 2.38 mm/s (stable)\\n- Days 16-31: Mean 3.15 mm/s (32% increase)\\n- Overall trend: +59% from start to end of month\\n\\n**COMP-001 Trend**:\\n- Days 1-15: Mean 3.85 mm/s (baseline)\\n- Days 16-31: Mean 5.15 mm/s (34% increase)\\n- Overall trend: +65% from start to end of month\\n\\n### 4.6 Correlation Analysis\\n\\n![Correlation Heatmap](images/correlation_heatmap.png)\\n\\nCorrelation matrix reveals key relationships:\\n\\n| Pair | Correlation | Interpretation |\\n|------|-------------|----------------|\\n| Vibration - Peak Accel | 0.94 | Strong mechanical coupling |\\n| RPM - Temperature | 0.81 | Speed-driven heating |\\n| RPM - Load | 0.79 | Operational coupling |\\n| Temperature - Load | 0.72 | Load-driven heating |\\n| Vibration - RPM | 0.49 | Moderate speed dependence |\\n| Vibration - Temperature | 0.13 | Weak direct coupling |\\n| Vibration - Load | 0.31 | Mild load dependence |\\n\\n**Interpretation**: The weak vibration-temperature correlation (r=0.13) indicates these sensors capture independent failure mechanisms, validating the multi-sensor monitoring approach. Vibration primarily reflects mechanical condition while temperature reflects thermal/loading state.\\n\\n