porary load reduction if vibration exceeds 7 mm/s\\n\\n2. **PUMP-002 Assessment**\\n   - Perform targeted vibration measurement at bearing locations\\n   - Check for cavitation indicators\\n   - Review recent maintenance history\\n\\n### 6.2 Short-Term Actions (Within 1 Month)\\n\\n3. **Enhanced Monitoring Protocol**\\n   - Increase sampling frequency to 15-minute intervals for COMP-001 and PUMP-002\\n   - Implement automated alerting at 2-sigma above asset-specific baselines\\n   - Add weekly trend review to operations meeting agenda\\n\\n4. **Zone-B Focus**\\n   - Conduct thermal imaging survey of all Zone-B assets\\n   - Verify sensor calibration for Zone-B installations\\n\\n### 6.3 Ongoing Strategy\\n\\n5. **Threshold Development**\\n   - Establish asset-specific alert thresholds based on historical baselines\\n   - Recommended initial thresholds:\\n     - COMP-001: Alert at 5.5 mm/s, Critical at 7.0 mm/s\\n     - PUMP-002: Alert at 3.5 mm/s, Critical at 4.5 mm/s\\n     - Other assets: Alert at mean + 2*std\\n\\n6. **Quarterly Review Cadence**\\n   - Repeat this analysis quarterly\\n   - Track degradation rates for trend assets\\n   - Update maintenance priorities based on latest data\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Conclusion\\n\\nThis analysis of 31 days of vibration and thermal telemetry reveals two assets (COMP-001, PUMP-002) requiring priority maintenance attention. The multi-sensor approach successfully identified degradation patterns not evident from single-metric monitoring. Implementation of the recommended actions will support risk-ranked maintenance prioritization and improved operational reliability.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Appendix A: Statistical Summary\\n\\nAll numerical results derived from code execution on sensor_panel_timeseries.csv. Analysis performed using Python with pandas, numpy, matplotlib, and seaborn libraries.\\n\\n**Report Generated**: October 2025 Monitoring Cycle\\n**Analysis Period**: 2025-10-01 to 2025-10-31\\n**Total Observations**: 5,952\\n')"
